    "why_capped": [
      "The cap is a CPU wall-clock decision, not a data or method decision. Measured training throughput is ~3.9 img/s at 352x256 width 16, so a full 9,128-slice epoch costs ~39 min of training plus validation.",
      "At 2,560 slices an epoch costs ~11-13 min, which made a 12-epoch run fit in ~2.6 h and a 30-epoch run in ~3.9 h.",
      "The cap is passed as max_train_slices; nothing in the architecture, split or preprocessing requires it."
    ],
    "critical_flaw": "The sampling RNG is seeded once per run, not per epoch, and the DataLoader is constructed once before training. The SAME 2,560 slices are therefore reused for every epoch - shuffling only reorders them. The remaining 6,568 training slices (72% of the available training data) were never seen by either completed run.",
    "leakage_status": "No leakage. Sampling draws exclusively from rows where split == 'train', and build_dataloaders asserts the splits are patient-disjoint on every construction."
  },
